{
  "contract_version": "2026-11-06.1",
  "about": [
    "The rules that decide what a conversation is called, and which row holds it.",
    "",
    "Three implementations keep them: the server (a Python rule and a MySQL CASE),",
    "the CLI (a JavaScript rule and a SQLite CASE), and the App (a Dart rule).",
    "They were written separately and they drifted. This file is the one place the",
    "cases live; each repository holds a copy and a test that checks its own",
    "implementation against it. The copies are pinned by checksum, so a change to",
    "the cases has to be made in every repository at once.",
    "",
    "What is in here, and who answers it:",
    "",
    "  placeholders  - which titles mean \"we have no name\". The server, the CLI",
    "                 and the App all answer it.",
    "  title_merges - which title a row keeps when a report arrives. The server",
    "                 and the CLI answer it; the App does not write titles.",
    "  survivors    - which row of a group of rows holds the conversation. The",
    "                 server and the CLI answer it; the App never picks a row.",
    "",
    "The cases are well-formed. A report that carries the custom flag with no title",
    "is not one of them: the flag describes a name, and a report with no name has",
    "no flag. The three implementations disagreed about that one shape and none of",
    "them can be reached by a report a device sends, so the server and the CLI",
    "normalise it away at the boundary instead of answering it here."
  ],
  "placeholders": [
